anv: AV1 BRC loop filter back-annotation on Xe2 (on top of 0015)

Under CBR/VBR the HuC update kernel now also picks the loop filter levels for the base_q_idx it chooses
(UPD_EnableLFUpdate, as media-driver always does; off for intra block copy frames). The frame header then
carries loop_filter_level[2..3] only when the chosen luma levels are not both zero, so its length is known
only on the GPU: the padding OBU and tile group header are recorded for both lengths in second level batches,
and the one matching the kernel's AVP_INLOOP_FILTER_STATE levels runs (MI_CONDITIONAL_BATCH_BUFFER_END); the
tile group obu_size store after PAK picks its address the same way.
vk_video: the header layout's size_in_bits now ends after trailing_one_bit (the HuC rewrites over that many
bits and only zero-pads: without the one bit the header has no trailing_one_bit, byte aligned it grows a byte).
CDEF stays as the application set it (ffmpeg's sequence header has enable_cdef = 0).

